# YAGO 4.5 taxonomy sample (N-Triples). Hand-authored; not a redistribution.
# rdfs:subClassOf edges + ys:fromClass provenance back to the Wikidata class.
# Prefixes (expanded inline, as N-Triples requires):
#   schema: http://schema.org/
#   yago:   http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/
#   ys:     http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#
#   wd:     http://www.wikidata.org/entity/
#   rdfs:   http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#

# --- classes that map onto the canonical schema (ys:fromClass -> Wikidata QID) ---
<http://schema.org/Language> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q34770> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/WritingSystem> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q8192> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/Culture> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11042> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/ArchaeologicalCulture> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q465299> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/ArtMovement> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q968159> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/LiteraryMovement> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2198855> .
<http://schema.org/Place> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2221906> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/Religion> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q9174> .

# --- schema.org top classes with no canonical-schema counterpart ---
<http://schema.org/Person> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5> .
<http://schema.org/Organization> <http://yago-knowledge.org/schema#fromClass> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q43229> .

# --- rdfs:subClassOf edges (the class hierarchy) ---
# both ends map to the corpus, already in datalog/taxonomy/subclass_of.tsv (redundant):
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/ArchaeologicalCulture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/Culture> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/LiteraryMovement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/ArtMovement> .
# both ends map to the corpus, NOT yet in our artifact (novel edge YAGO would add):
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/ArtMovement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/Culture> .
# one end maps, the super-class is an unmapped schema.org top class (partial):
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/Culture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://schema.org/Intangible> .
<http://schema.org/Language> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://schema.org/Intangible> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/WritingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://schema.org/CreativeWork> .
<http://yago-knowledge.org/resource/Religion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://schema.org/Intangible> .
# neither end maps (schema.org internal hierarchy the corpus does not model):
<http://schema.org/Person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://schema.org/Thing> .
<http://schema.org/Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://schema.org/Thing> .
